# How to design for Signoff

A checklist for designers (human or otherwise) making new mockups in the Signoff system.

## Before you start

1. **Read `README.md`.** Every fundamental is listed there.
2. **Pick the right surface.** Is this a new agent/chat flow, a Command Center widget, a settings page, or a modal? Each has a distinct layout.
3. **Pull tokens in.** Link `assets/colors_and_type.css` at the top of your HTML. Do not redefine colors or fonts.

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/base.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/colors_and_type.css">
```

## Do

- **Use Ant Design components as your baseline.** Button, Input, Select, Card, Table, Tag, Menu, Layout. Style overrides go through the tokens in `theme.js`, not inline `!important`.
- **Use Lucide icons.** Pick from: `Command, Sparkles, IndianRupee, Calendar, Settings, Send, Brain, Bookmark, Trash2, Download, ChevronLeft, ChevronRight, Plus, Save, X, ExternalLink, TrendingUp, FileText, DollarSign, Zap, Loader2`.
- **Keep the primary blue rare.** It goes on the main CTA per view, the selected nav item (subtle tinted background using `--signoff-blue-tint-06` plus blue label text — no ink bar, no right-border accent), links, and focus rings. That's it. The same active-state treatment is used for the Settings page's vertical tab rail so all nav surfaces feel consistent.
- **Respect the density.** 32px controls, 14px body, 16px gaps. The UI is calm and tight â€” resist blowing things up.
- **Match the chat pattern.** Bot avatar left, user avatar right, rounded bubbles with a tighter corner on the speaker's side (`border-top-right-radius: 6px` for user, mirror for bot).

## Don't

- Don't introduce new colors, fonts, or icon families.
- Don't add dark mode.
- Don't use emoji in-UI. The only image is the logo.
- Don't make anything full-width edge-to-edge â€” the content column is capped at `1700px` and most chat/input at `800px`.
- Don't animate with bounces, springs, or anything over 300ms.
- Don't use pill-shaped buttons (border-radius: 999px) unless it's a chip or a circular FAB.
- Don't stack shadows. One shadow per element, period.

## Patterns worth copying verbatim

### App shell
Fixed sider (240px expanded / 80px collapsed) on `#fafafa`. Fixed top header (64px) on `#ffffff`. Content area with rounded top-left corner, max-width 1700, centered.

### Chat landing page
Centered column. Small chip badge ("AI-Powered Analytics" with `Zap` icon) â†’ Poppins 40px greeting ("Hi {firstName}") â†’ 16px tagline â†’ stack of prompt cards â†’ input wrapper at bottom with textarea + Deep Research toggle + Mic + Send.

### Prompt card
Glassy white (`rgba(255,255,255,0.8)`), 12px radius, 32px icon well tinted primary, bookmark/delete action on the right, arrow `â†’` glyph that slides on hover.

### Message bubble
- User: gradient `#3b82f6 â†’ #1d4ed8`, white text, 16px radius with 6px on the speaker corner, max-width 70%.
- Bot: transparent background, no padding, just the avatar (28px) + text + timestamp + Save as PDF button.
- Thinking: three `#3b82f6` dots that pulse at 1.4s.

### Follow-up queries
Soft tinted blue pill buttons under the bot message, with a `â†—` glyph and a save-to-bookmark icon beside each.

### Pinned widget card
Full-height card with a header row (title + View All link) and a body (chart, table, or list). On hover, lift 1px.

